description:
Combine lessons 5.03 and 5.04 into the model behind a real inspector: several objects selected, fields shown as one value or mixed, drags that edit live but create one undo step, undo and redo, and a dirty flag for the title bar.

```cpp
class Inspector
{
public:
    void addObject(int id, std::map<std::string, double> fields);
    void select(std::vector<int> ids);                      // ids that do not exist are ignored
    std::string shown(const std::string& field) const;     // lesson 5.03's rules over the selection

    void beginEdit(const std::string& field);               // like IsItemActivated: a drag starts
    void editValue(const std::string& field, double value); // every frame of the drag: write live
    void endEdit();                                         // like IsItemDeactivatedAfterEdit

    bool undo();
    bool redo();
    std::string undoLabel() const;                          // "Undo Change range" or "" (see below)
    double value(int id, const std::string& field) const;  // NaN if the object or field does not exist
    void markSaved();
    bool dirty() const;
};
```

**Editing.**

- `beginEdit(field)` remembers the current value of `field` for every selected object that has it.
- `editValue(field, v)` writes `v` to that field on every selected object that has it, immediately, so the view updates during the drag.
- `endEdit()` records **one** undo step that takes every affected object from its remembered value to its current value. If nothing changed (every value is what it was), it records nothing.
- `editValue` called **without** a `beginEdit` for that field (a checkbox click, a value typed in) applies and records its own one-step change at once.
- The step's label is `Change <field>` for one object, or `Change <field> (<n> objects)` for several.
- The selection at the time of the edit is part of the step: undoing after the selection changed still restores the right objects.

**Undo, redo and dirty** follow lesson 5.04's practice (a new step clears redo; dirty compares the current position with the saved one; there is no limit here).

